config PIPAR_WATCHDOG_FEEDER
    bool "Pipar recovery watchdog feeder"
    default n
    depends on TASK_WDT && WATCHDOG
    help
      Feeds a task watchdog from the system workqueue so the device
      auto-resets if the workqueue hangs (e.g., a stuck I2C transfer
      or any work handler that never returns).

config PIPAR_WATCHDOG_TASK_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Task watchdog timeout (ms)"
    default 8000
    range 1000 30000
    depends on PIPAR_WATCHDOG_FEEDER
    help
      If the system workqueue doesn't feed the watchdog within this
      timeout, the device resets.

config PIPAR_WATCHDOG_FEED_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Watchdog feed interval (ms)"
    default 2000
    range 100 10000
    depends on PIPAR_WATCHDOG_FEEDER
    help
      How often the feeder schedules itself to feed the watchdog.
      Should be substantially less than the task timeout to allow
      for normal workqueue jitter.
